<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Sepap H1 consol. profit drops.</title>
<headline>Czech Sepap H1 consol. profit drops.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary unaudited results for six-month period ending June 30, 1996 (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> pre-tax profit		195.064   vs   875.047</p>
<p> operating profit	    303.513   vs 1,024.916</p>
<p>sales of own goods and</p>
<p> services		    3,023.508	3,521.306</p>
<p> assets			7,994.193	7,239.721</p>
<p> basic capital	     3,427.168	2,762.168</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Sepap a.s. a holding company for pulp and paper operations. In the latest disclosure from the Central Securities Registry on August 28, the Daventree group held a 47 percent stake in Sepap, and Swedish paper group AssiDomaen held a 39 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Radek Narovec, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
